<title>SINGAPORE: Thakral first half net profit up 20 pct.</title>
<headline>Thakral first half net profit up 20 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to September 30 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore $ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		  28.67    vs    23.89</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)	5.39    vs     6.02</p>
<p>    Turnover		   552.09    vs   568.97</p>
<p>    Profit before tax	 34.86    vs    29.43</p>
<p>    Associates		  25.82    vs    23.89</p>
<p>    Interest expense	   7.33    vs     8.69</p>
<p>    Other income		 1.98    vs     0.26</p>
<p>    Tax			    6.57    vs     5.38</p>
<p>    Minorities	   gain  0.37    vs     0.16 loss</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries    loss  2.85    vs     nil</p>
<p>Note - Consumer electronics group Thakral Corp said the extraordinaries loss came from Wearnes Thakral Pte Ltd and was related to a succession of manufacturing activities and restructuring of business.--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
